---
import { ArrowUpRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
import { loadCorpus } from '../lib/corpus';
import { breadcrumbs, graph, organization, website } from '../lib/schema';

const corpus = await loadCorpus();

const trail = [
	{ name: 'Home', path: '/' },
	{ name: 'About', path: '/about' },
];

const jsonLd = graph(organization(), website(), breadcrumbs(trail));
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Who operates BestInsurance Research, how it is funded, what it is for, and the boundary between it, Bollinsure, CovWell, and BestAMS."
	jsonLd={jsonLd}
	pageType="editorial"
>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="About"
		title="Who runs this, and why that matters to you"
		lede="An insurance brokerage operates a public advisory instrument and research library. That is a real commercial relationship, and the only honest way to handle it is to state it on every page and design the site so it cannot quietly become a lead funnel."
		trail={trail}
	/>

	<section class="band band-tight">
		<div class="shell answer-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2 id="operator">The operator</h2>
				<p>
					BestInsurance Research is operated by <strong>{siteConfig.operator.legalName}</strong>,
					doing business as <strong>{siteConfig.operator.dba}</strong>, a California insurance
					brokerage. Its {siteConfig.operator.licenseAuthority} agency licence number is{' '}
					<span class="num">{siteConfig.operator.agencyLicense}</span>.
				</p>
				<p>Licensed producers:</p>
				<ul>
					{
						siteConfig.operator.producers.map((producer) => (
							<li>
								{producer.name}, California licence <span class="num">{producer.license}</span>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
				<p>
					This site is not a regulator, a rating agency, an insurer, or an independent consumer
					organization, and it does not present itself as any of those. It is a public advisory
					instrument and research library published by a brokerage.
				</p>

				<h2 id="why">Why it exists</h2>
				<p>
					Most insurance information online is written to capture a lead. The tell is structural: the
					answer is thin, the sources are absent or decorative, and the real payload is a form. That
					pattern trains people to distrust the whole category, including the parts that would
					actually help them.
				</p>
				<p>
					The alternative is a library that answers the question completely, shows its evidence,
					states its uncertainty, and lets you leave. If that is genuinely useful, some readers will
					later choose to work with a broker, and some of those will choose this one. That is a
					slower and more defensible way to earn the work than gating an answer behind an email
					field.
				</p>

				<h2 id="promise">The promise</h2>
				<blockquote style="border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); padding-left: var(--s-4); margin: var(--s-5) 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-xl); color: var(--ink); line-height: var(--leading-snug)">
					Ask an insurance question. See the answer, the evidence, the uncertainty, and the next
					responsible step.
				</blockquote>
				<p>
					All four parts matter. An answer without evidence is an opinion. Evidence without a stated
					uncertainty is overconfidence. And a next step that is always "contact us" is a funnel
					wearing a library's clothes.
				</p>

				<h2 id="boundary">Where this sits</h2>
				<p>Four things exist, and keeping them distinct is deliberate.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>BestInsurance Research</strong>, this site, attracts, explains, cites, and
						organizes public information. It collects nothing.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Bollinsure</strong> handles identified client intake, licensed advice, quoting,
						uploads, appointments, email, and calls. Everything personal happens there, under its own
						disclosed terms.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>CovWell</strong> is the insured-facing self-guided coverage and service product.
						It is not a second research library or advisory instrument, and it is outside this site.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>BestAMS</strong> is Bollinsure's private system of record. Nothing on this site
						reads from it, writes to it, or is trained on it.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<Callout tone="note">
					<p>
						<strong>{siteConfig.licensedHelpDisclosure}</strong> Bollinsure may be compensated by an
						insurer when it places coverage. It is not the only source of licensed help: you can
						work with any licensed broker or agent, or contact an insurer directly.
					</p>
				</Callout>
				<p>
					The research journey never requires a handoff. Every answer, its full source ledger, and
					its stated limits are complete whether or not you ever click a Bollinsure link.
				</p>

				<h2 id="corpus">What is published so far</h2>
				<p>
					The library is deliberately small and deep rather than large and thin. There are{' '}
					{corpus.questions.length} canonical questions, {corpus.coverages.length} coverage pages,{' '}
					{corpus.companies.length} organization records, {corpus.states.length} state pages,{' '}
					{corpus.examples.length} labeled examples, {corpus.liveTools.length} tools, and{' '}
					{corpus.sources.length} source records behind them.
				</p>
				<p>
					Lines and jurisdictions that are not published yet are named as gaps on{' '}
					<a href="/insurance">the coverage index</a> and <a href="/states">the states index</a>,
					with no route and no sitemap entry, rather than published as empty pages. Tools that are
					specified but not built stay in <a href="/tools">the registry</a> for the same reason.
				</p>

				<h2 id="podcast">Speaking of Insurance</h2>
				<p>
					Bollinsure publishes a podcast, <em>{siteConfig.podcast.name}</em>. Its canonical feed is
					hosted on Transistor and its canonical episode archive lives on Bollinsure. This site does
					not mirror the feed, does not compete with that archive, and does not import transcripts as
					research pages.
				</p>
				<p>
					An episode may be cited here when it materially supports an answer, with a direct link to
					the canonical Bollinsure episode page and a clear source label. A transcript enters the
					corpus only after factual review, source mapping, and segmentation into claims, exactly
					like any other source.
				</p>

				<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Corrections and source reports:{' '}
						<a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						Licensed help, offered separately and optionally:{' '}
						<a href={siteConfig.bollinsureOrigin} rel="noopener">
							{siteConfig.operator.dba} <ArrowUpRight size={13} aria-hidden="true" style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-2px" />
						</a>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<aside class="answer-rail" aria-label="Page contents">
				<nav class="rail-block" aria-labelledby="on-this-page">
					<h2 id="on-this-page">On this page</h2>
					<ol>
						<li><a href="#operator">The operator</a></li>
						<li><a href="#why">Why it exists</a></li>
						<li><a href="#promise">The promise</a></li>
						<li><a href="#boundary">Where this sits</a></li>
						<li><a href="#corpus">What is published</a></li>
						<li><a href="#podcast">Speaking of Insurance</a></li>
						<li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
					</ol>
				</nav>
				<div class="rail-block">
					<h2>Operator</h2>
					<dl>
						<div><dt>Legal name</dt><dd>{siteConfig.operator.legalName}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Doing business as</dt><dd>{siteConfig.operator.dba}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Agency licence</dt><dd class="num">{siteConfig.operator.agencyLicense}</dd></div>
						<div><dt>Regulator</dt><dd>{siteConfig.operator.licenseAuthority}</dd></div>
					</dl>
				</div>
				<div class="rail-block no-print">
					<h2>People</h2>
					<ul>
						{corpus.people.map((person) => <li><a href={`/authors/${person.id}`}>{person.data.name}</a></li>)}
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="rail-block no-print">
					<h2>Standards</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><a href="/methodology">Methodology</a></li>
						<li><a href="/editorial-policy">Editorial policy</a></li>
						<li><a href="/corrections">Corrections</a></li>
						<li><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></li>
						<li><a href="/terms">Terms</a></li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
